5,1,1,talk,Midori,,I worry about who owns the system when it breaks. Let’s check support ownership during last winter's outage.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,The yard devices are old. I need to see the 2021 scheduling trial to understand hardware limits.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,May,,I’m concerned about systems that quietly age. I’ll look at the upgrade history of the dispatch tool.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Misaki,,I need to know who is left to carry the load. I’ll check administrator retirements and hiring times.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,I care about the bill that keeps arriving. I’ll look at five years of renewal invoices.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, if the hardware fails, does the vendor fix it? That’s part of ownership too.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, yes. If the vendor can’t touch our old terminals, the system is useless on the floor.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, do the invoices show a pattern of emergency fixes? That tells me about decay.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, decay hits the people who have to patch it. I’m watching the staffing gaps.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, exactly. I’m looking for the line items that appear only after the contract is signed.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Midori,,I also want to see the depot calendar. Peak season cutover is where plans usually break.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,Agreed. The calendar dictates when we can actually test. I’ll check the depot calendar and the peak-season cutover.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,May,,I’ll also look at the data lift in the 2018 pay move. Bad migrations start there.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Misaki,,I’ll also check the depot supervisors and the last rollout. They know the real pain points.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,I’ll also look at the board minutes on capital and operating requests. That’s where the real budget lives.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Midori,,Let’s see what these records reveal. I hope we find a clear owner.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,I hope we find a system that doesn’t crash when the forklifts start moving.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,May,,I hope we find a system that doesn’t rot in the first year.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Misaki,,I hope we find a system that doesn’t break the people who run it.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,I hope we find a system that doesn’t break the bank after the handshake.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
