60,3,1,talk,Midori,,I’m leaning toward D. The on-site engineering team means someone is actually there when things break. That solves the ownership problem.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,I agree with @Midori. D is built for transport and runs on our own servers. It will work with our old hardware and fit our calendar.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,I’m also leaning toward D. The on-site team can handle upgrades and migrations properly. It won’t rot in place.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
